values ('bbbb0004-0000-4000-8000-00000000003d', 'en', null, 'Astrophysics', 'Astrophysics is the branch of physics that explains the stars, galaxies, and the universe as a whole, from how we gather starlight to what the cosmos is actually made of. This course walks from the electromagnetic spectrum and stellar life cycles through cosmology, dark matter, exoplanets, and gravitational waves, explaining the math in plain words and ASCII formulas. The structure and topics are adapted from the overview article at Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia (CC BY-SA 4.0).', null, 'foundations', 59, true, 'science', '{}')
